---
/**
 * C-2 · Context summary — Topic / Regarding. `CONTACT_WIREFRAME.md` C-2
 * (Page IA Stage B), "**the page's signature responsibility**".
 *
 * Component (Inventory): Context Summary Block — on Contact, the **Topic
 * Summary**. Responsibility realized: "show the visitor that the architecture
 * already knows why they are here — **continuity of context**."
 *
 * Spatial composition, transcribed: "a calm, reassuring acknowledgement placed
 * **before** the form … **Understated, never a banner or a sell.** When no
 * context carried over, it degrades gracefully to the neutral broad-Topic
 * framing (default **'Not sure'**), never an empty or awkward slot."
 *
 * ── WHY THE SERVER RENDERS THE NEUTRAL STATE, ALWAYS ───────────────────────
 * The site is 100% prerendered (§6.1) and the prefill lives in the query string,
 * which no build-time render can read. So this module ships in its neutral state
 * on every load and the island upgrades it in place when `?topic=`/`?regarding=`
 * resolve. That ordering is not a compromise — the neutral state is a SPECIFIED
 * state, it is the majority arrival (Homepage, global nav, search all carry no
 * prefill per `CONTACT_PAGE_IA.md` §"Prefill sources"), and a visitor with no JS
 * sees a complete, correct, unapologetic version of this module rather than a
 * gap.
 *
 * ── NOTHING FROM THE URL IS EVER PRINTED HERE ──────────────────────────────
 * The templates below carry `{service}` and `{topic}` placeholders, and the
 * island fills them from the RESOLVED prefill — an authored Service name and a
 * Pillar label, both matched out of the CMS catalogue by `prefill.ts`. An
 * unrecognised parameter resolves to nothing and this module stays neutral,
 * which is §23.1's "ignored rather than echoed" made visible.
 *
 * No live region. This module reaches its final state during page load, before
 * anyone is reading it; announcing it would interrupt with something the visitor
 * is about to read anyway.
 */
import type { ContactMessages } from '../../lib/i18n/contact';

interface Props {
  copy: ContactMessages['context'];
}

const { copy } = Astro.props;
---

<p class="c-context rv" data-rv="meta" data-context>
  <span class="c-context-label">{copy.label}</span>
  <span
    class="c-context-value"
    data-context-value
    data-neutral={copy.neutral}
    data-topic-only={copy.topicOnly}
    data-with-service={copy.withService}>{copy.neutral}</span
  >
</p>
